From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Miguel Salinas <mikeys@me.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:13:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat(durable): readStoredContext derives a conversation's
 context from Storage alone

Conversation.context({ at }) needs an open Harness. A process that only reads
a session another process drives (to fork it at an earlier entry, or to show
it) has the Storage but no Harness of its own, and had to copy the derivation:
the newest head marker, edits, excluded stop reasons, system message lead and
tool result ordering, and keep the copy in step with Pi.

readStoredContext(storage, conversationId, context, { at }) runs the same
derivation over Storage reads only (ContextStorage: entry, findLatestHeadMarker,
scanEntries) and returns the view Conversation.context() returns.
